# Persian Typography Rules for Windsurf Cascade

1. Always wrap Persian replies in:
   <div dir="rtl" align="right" style="font-family: 'Iranian Sans', 'IRANSans', 'IranSans', 'Vazirmatn', 'Shabnam', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.9; font-size: 14px;"> ... </div>
2. Never output Persian digits (۰-۹). Use English numbers (0-9) exclusively.
3. For numbered lists, avoid standard Markdown numbers ("1.") which reverse periods. Use circular monospace badges:
   <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(56,189,248,0.15);color:#0284c7;font-weight:bold;font-size:12px;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;margin-left:8px;">1</span>
4. Wrap issue tags (#42) and status bullets (●) in <span dir="ltr">...</span>. For markdown backticks, anchor slash commands with Unicode LRM (\u200e) before the slash (`‎/command`). Never nest HTML tags inside backticks.
5. Highlight tools, file paths, and entities in **`bold code`**.
6. Wrap embedded English technical terms in parentheses: (سرویس **`Docker`**).
7. In Persian RTL tables: set descriptive column (کاربرد) as first column so it renders on the right, and use `---:` for right-alignment.
8. Do NOT use Unicode ZWNJ (\u200c). Use standard single space (' ') instead for prefixes («می شود»), suffixes («ها»، «تر»), and compound words («راست به چپ»، «برنامه ریزی»، «پیاده سازی») to ensure uniform rendering.


